A microstructure-cleaning study needs two success criteria (@cm-mems-damage: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Particle-Removal-and-MEMS-Damage-Hirano.lingua#r_0RH4K2MTZZG42NZ4MMZE1K6G9E", #source "../sources/Cleaning-Technology-in-Semiconductor-Device-Manufacturing-VIII.lingua#r_1CVF9XCJR7E3J37X5150BDS5Y2", #clean-manufacturing "A-particle-map-can-saturate-before-the-particles-disappear.lingua#r_2Y4R7MPT73HD67YPG6PFFA27JB") { r_0Z5WZVMSW07NRCZPC96C84F4S9
**Read:** [Particle removal and MEMS damage — Hirano and colleagues](../sources/Particle-Removal-and-MEMS-Damage-Hirano.lingua#r_0RH4K2MTZZG42NZ4MMZE1K6G9E) and the English microstructure and megasonic articles in [Cleaning technology in semiconductor device manufacturing VIII — ECS proceedings](../sources/Cleaning-Technology-in-Semiconductor-Device-Manufacturing-VIII.lingua#r_1CVF9XCJR7E3J37X5150BDS5Y2), printed pages 145–182.

Define success using both contaminant reduction and retained function. A test particle population, an unpatterned wafer and a fragile structure probe different aspects of a process. The treatment that performs well on one specimen can fail on another.

A comparison needs initial contamination, detection limits, damaged-feature definitions, sampled area, replicates and preparation history. A clean image after processing cannot distinguish successful cleaning from loss of the feature that held the particle unless the structure is also measured.

**Work:** Reconstruct the study's particle and structural observations separately. Compare aqueous chemistry with physical assistance while holding the relevant sample state fixed. State which results are demonstrated for the published system and which are extrapolations. Add a functional observation beyond microscopy for a proposed new device.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
